@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: stable
+entities: [Post]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/HomeController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/PostResource.ts
+  - app/Http/Validators/PostValidator.ts
+  - app/Console/Commands/ScheduledPostsCommand.ts
+  - bin/console.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-fable/5.1", at: 2026-09-25T05:38:49.551Z }
+---
+
+# Scheduled publishing via published_at
+
+## Context
+
+Authors write ahead of time, but a post went live the moment it was saved,
+so launch posts were kept in documents and pasted in by hand. Editorial
+wants to write now and publish later; ops wants to read the calendar from a
+terminal.
+
+## Decision
+
+- `posts.published_at` is a nullable ISO 8601 UTC text column, stored like
+  `created_at`. `NULL` or a past instant means public; a future instant means
+  scheduled. Nothing runs at publish time: visibility is decided per request
+  by comparing the column against the current time.
+- The form field is `publishAt` on `posts.store` and `posts.update`. It is
+  optional and nullable; any offset it carries is normalised to UTC before
+  storage so the column compares as plain text.
+- `Post.visibleTo(viewerId)` is the single query filter for the list, search
+  and home page: public posts plus the viewer's own. `Post.isScheduled()` is
+  the per-record check the show action uses.
+- A scheduled post answers 404, not 403, to everyone but its author, so the
+  id's existence is not confirmed.
+- `posts:scheduled` prints `<id>\t<title>\t<published_at>` soonest first and
+  nothing else on stdout; `bin/console.ts` routes boot logging to stderr so
+  the output pipes cleanly.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Publishing needs no scheduler, queue or cron entry, and cannot fire early
+  or late relative to the request that reads the post.
+- The lexicographic `<=` comparison relies on every stored value being in the
+  same UTC ISO 8601 format. Writes go through the validator and normaliser;
+  direct database writes must keep that format.
+- Unpublishing a live post is only possible by giving it a future date, and
+  a post carries at most one date.
